{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4596744","formula":"C₁₃H₂₈O","hill":"C13H28O","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"H":28.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"2,2,4,4-Tetramethyl-3-t-butyl-pentane-3-ol"},"descriptions":{"en":"2,2,4,4-Tetramethyl-3-t-butyl-pentane-3-ol or tri-tert-butylcarbinol is an organic compound with formula C13H28O, ((H3C)3C)3COH, or tBu3COH. It is an alcohol that can be viewed as a structural analog of a tridecane isomer (2,2,4,4-tetramethyl-3-t-butylpentane) where the central hydrogen has been replaced by a hydroxyl group -OH. Tri-tert-butylcarbinol is arguably the most sterically hindered alcohol that has been prepared to date. In contrast to all other known alcohols, the infrared spectrum of the liquid does not exhibit a broad OH absorption associated with intermolecular hydrogen bonding, making it interesting for research in spectroscopy."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":142558,"mass":200.36,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(C)(C)C(C(C)(C)C)(C(C)(C)C)O","inchikey":"LIUBOLYWYDGCSJ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"3-tert-butyl-2,2,4,4-tetramethylpentan-3-ol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"142558","atoms":42,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.046,"y":0.038,"z":-1.78,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.006,"y":0.007,"z":-0.325,"el":"C"},{"x":1.275,"y":0.983,"z":0.097,"el":"C"},{"x":0.196,"y":-1.599,"z":0.052,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.505,"y":0.632,"z":0.054,"el":"C"},{"x":2.656,"y":0.246,"z":0.066,"el":"C"},{"x":1.517,"y":2.14,"z":-0.908,"el":"C"},{"x":1.146,"y":1.639,"z":1.487,"el":"C"},{"x":0.4,"y":-1.855,"z":1.569,"el":"C"},{"x":1.498,"y":-2.231,"z":-0.54,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.982,"y":-2.498,"z":-0.378,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.568,"y":2.174,"z":0.032,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.648,"y":0.113,"z":-0.88,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.025,"y":0.211,"z":1.455,"el":"C"},{"x":2.879,"y":-0.19,"z":-0.91,"el":"H"},{"x":3